From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 7 May 2026 10:41:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?dos:=20Phase=2010=20patch=200044=20=E2=80=94=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?skip=20MPU-401=20probe=20by=20default=20(real-HW)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

W22-WB-D operator iter (2026-05-07) confirmed the 0042 defensive
probe still hangs system on real Vibra16S+S2. WBSDL.LOG ended at
exactly the line "mpu401: probe entry port_base=0x0330" — the 0042
entry log line wrote successfully (per-line fsync committed it to
disk) but the very next inportb (status register read at port_base
+1) hung the ISA bus. CPU never saw the read complete; the 0042
iteration counter never advanced because the inportb itself blocks
the bus.

The probe approach is fundamentally incompatible with this chip.
Defensive iteration caps don't help when the very first inb is
the lockup point. Architectural change required: SKIP the probe
entirely for the default code path.

New default behavior in SDL_DOSMpu401Init: BLIND init.

  - Write the UART mode entry command (0x3F) to port_base+1
    without any read or ACK polling.
  - Mark backend ready unconditionally.
  - Return true.

Failure modes:
  - Chip present + responsive: subsequent MIDI byte writes produce
    sound. WB backend works.
  - Chip absent / not seated: MIDI byte writes go to a non-decoding
    port. Music is silent. NO LOCK because there's no read on the
    lockup-prone status register. Failing-to-silence beats failing-
    to-lockup.

This is the "trust the user" pattern matching the 1990s convention:
when AUDIO_BACKEND=wb is explicitly declared (or the auto-detect
chain selects WB), the user takes responsibility for hardware
presence. The driver's job is to not crash the system when the
hardware isn't there.

Probe path retained behind SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_PROBE_MPU401=1
opt-in for diagnosis on hardware known-safe to probe (DOSBox-X
emulated MPU-401, hypothetical future ISA chips that don't stall
the bus on cold reads). Strict-1 env-var match per CLAUDE.md
convention. Default OFF: even auto-detect chain gets blind init
(fail-open semantics).

Implementation: same SDL_DOSMpu401Init function signature as 0042;
the probe-vs-blind branch is at function entry. Probe path code
preserved verbatim from 0042 (open-bus early-exit + iteration
cap) — readable diff as a single conditional block rather than
new function. Engine-side calls don't change; the SDL hint
controls behavior internally.

doskutsu_dbg_log lines:
  - blind init path: "mpu401: blind init at port_base=0x%04x ..."
  - probe path: existing 4 lines from 0042 (entry/early-exit/
    fail/ok) preserved.

BOOT.md entry added per env_vars_document_in_user_docs.md:
  SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_PROBE_MPU401=1
  Category: dev-only (LOCKUP RISK on real Vibra16S+S2; opt-in
  for diagnosis on emulated or known-safe hardware only).

Validation: DOSBox-X smoke gates "doesn't break organya" + "blind
WB init produces MIDI dispatch under DOSBox-X's MPU-401 emulation".
Real-HW iter on g2k Vibra16S+S2 is the actual gate per memory
dosbox_not_behavioral_proxy_for_io.md. Don't claim fix works
until operator runs it.
---
 src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c | 98 +++++++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 68 insertions(+), 30 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c b/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c
index e1bb0555a..a5509d3cd 100644
--- a/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c
+++ b/src/core/dos/SDL_dos_audio_synth.c
@@ -62,17 +62,72 @@ static int s_mpu401_port_base = -1;
 
 bool SDL_DOSMpu401Init(uint16_t port_base)
 {
-    doskutsu_dbg_log("mpu401: probe entry port_base=0x%04x", (unsigned)port_base);
-
-    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0042): open-bus early-exit. Read
-       the status register BEFORE issuing the reset write. If it returns
-       0xFF, that's the canonical "no chip is decoding this address" /
-       open-bus pattern on ISA — bail with false immediately rather than
-       writing reset to a non-responsive port. This avoids the W22-WB-C
-       lockup failure mode where issuing reset to a non-responsive chip
-       stalled the ISA bus indefinitely on real Vibra16S CT2490
-       (the failure was distinct from the inb-poll loop spinning; the
-       outportb write itself appears to have hung). */
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0044): SKIP the probe by default.
+
+       W22-WB-D real-HW evidence: WBSDL.LOG ended at exactly the line
+       "mpu401: probe entry port_base=0x0330" (the 0042 entry log line
+       wrote successfully + fsync committed it) — but the very next
+       inportb (status register read at port_base+1) hung the ISA bus
+       on real Vibra16S+S2. CPU never saw the read complete; the iter
+       counter from 0042 never advanced because the inportb itself
+       blocks the bus. The probe approach is fundamentally incompatible
+       with this hardware.
+
+       New default: BLIND init. Write the UART mode entry command
+       (0x3F) without any read or ACK polling. Mark backend ready
+       unconditionally. Return true.
+
+       Failure modes:
+         - Chip present + responsive: subsequent MIDI byte writes
+           produce sound. WB backend works.
+         - Chip absent / not seated: MIDI byte writes go to a non-
+           decoding port. Music is silent. NO LOCK because there's
+           no read on the lockup-prone status register.
+
+       This is the "trust the user" pattern: when the user explicitly
+       declares AUDIO_BACKEND=wb (or the auto-detect chain selects
+       WB), they take responsibility for hardware presence. Failing-
+       to-silence beats failing-to-lockup.
+
+       Probe path retained behind SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_PROBE_MPU401=1
+       for hardware known-safe to probe (e.g. DOSBox-X emulated
+       MPU-401, or hypothetical future ISA chips that don't stall
+       the bus on cold reads). Default OFF: even the auto-detect
+       chain gets blind init (fail-open semantics). Strict-1 env-var
+       match per CLAUDE.md convention. */
+    const char *probe_env = SDL_getenv("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_PROBE_MPU401");
+    const bool do_probe = (probe_env && probe_env[0] == '1' && probe_env[1] == 0);
+
+    if (!do_probe) {
+        doskutsu_dbg_log("mpu401: blind init at port_base=0x%04x "
+                         "(probe disabled — patch 0044 default; set "
+                         "SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_PROBE_MPU401=1 to enable "
+                         "probe path with LOCKUP RISK on real Vibra16S+S2)",
+                         (unsigned)port_base);
+        /* UART mode entry. After this, all writes to data port pass
+           directly to MIDI bus; status bit 6 (0x40) = DRR (data ready
+           to receive; must be 0 before each write — but we never read
+           it on this path; chip clocks data out on its own). */
+        outportb((Uint16)(port_base + 1), 0x3F);
+        s_mpu401_port_base = (int)port_base;
+        return true;
+    }
+
+    /* === Probe path (opt-in via SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_PROBE_MPU401=1) ===
+
+       LOCKUP RISK on real Vibra16S+S2 — see W22-WB-D postmortem.
+       Retained for diagnosis on emulated MPU-401 hardware (DOSBox-X)
+       or future chips known-safe to probe. Logic preserved from
+       patch 0042 (open-bus early-exit + iteration-cap). */
+    doskutsu_dbg_log("mpu401: probe entry port_base=0x%04x "
+                     "(SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_PROBE_MPU401=1; LOCKUP RISK)",
+                     (unsigned)port_base);
+
+    /* Open-bus early-exit (from patch 0042): if the status register
+       returns 0xFF on the very first read, that's canonical ISA
+       open-bus and we bail without issuing reset. Doesn't help if
+       the inportb itself stalls (the W22-WB-D failure mode), but
+       handles the no-chip-decoding-port case cleanly. */
     const Uint8 initial_status = inportb((Uint16)(port_base + 1));
     if (initial_status == 0xFF) {
         doskutsu_dbg_log("mpu401: probe early-exit (status=0xFF; no chip at 0x%04x)",
@@ -83,20 +138,7 @@ bool SDL_DOSMpu401Init(uint16_t port_base)
     /* Reset MPU-401: write 0xFF to command port (data + 1). */
     outportb((Uint16)(port_base + 1), 0xFF);
 
-    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 10 patch 0042): poll for ACK (0xFE) with a
-       hard ITERATION CAP rather than an SDL_GetTicksNS()-based wall-
-       clock deadline. The original 10ms deadline approach hung
-       indefinitely on real Vibra16S+S2 hardware in W22-WB-C iter (WB.LOG
-       ended at the engine-side "probing port..." line with no further
-       output, including no SDL-side log). Suspected: either ISA bus
-       stall on the status-port read, or a pathological interaction with
-       SDL3's timer source. The iteration cap is a known-bounded code
-       path that terminates regardless of timer-source state.
-
-       Sizing: 20000 iterations × ~500ns per inportb on Pentium ≈ 10ms
-       wall-clock — same upper bound as the original deadline, but
-       without the timer dependency. Status bit 7 (0x80) = DSR (data-
-       set-ready inverse: low = data available to read). */
+    /* Poll for ACK (0xFE) with hard iteration cap (from patch 0042). */
     bool ack_ok = false;
     int iter;
     for (iter = 0; iter < 20000; iter++) {
@@ -116,11 +158,7 @@ bool SDL_DOSMpu401Init(uint16_t port_base)
         return false;
     }
 
-    /* Enter UART mode. After this, all writes to data port pass
-       directly to MIDI bus; status bit 6 (0x40) = DRR (data ready
-       to receive; must be 0 before each write). Some clones don't
-       ACK the UART-mode command per docs/PHASE10-DESIGN.md § C.2
-       step 4; we don't require a second ACK. */
+    /* Enter UART mode. */
     outportb((Uint16)(port_base + 1), 0x3F);
     s_mpu401_port_base = (int)port_base;
     doskutsu_dbg_log("mpu401: probe ok (UART mode active at 0x%04x; "
-- 
